From 3258fc967a0112740e491f8d387dc011243d67c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:11:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] am: ListExistingContentInfosSystem; unimplemented-call log
 flood guard (Build 140)

The eShop's "Repair software" check (Gedownload > Software herstellen) asks
am:sys ListExistingContentInfosSystem (0x002B) for the title's contents.
Tangelo had no handler: the call was answered "success" with nothing in the
output buffer, after which the check looped on an unknown command (0x0C01)
on a file session about 14,000 times a second and filled the 100 MB log in
29 seconds.

- am:u/am:sys/am:net 0x002B ListExistingContentInfosSystem: inputs content
  count, media type, title ID, start index and a mapped buffer; returns the
  ContentInfo (index, type, content ID, size, ownership) of every content of
  the title's TMD whose file exists (and is not being imported), skipping
  the first start_index of those. Ownership: owned when the ticket gives
  rights (or there is no ticket), always downloaded. Logs
  "ListExistingContentInfosSystem: title ...: N content(s)".
- service.cpp ReportUnimplementedFunction: logs the first 10 calls of each
  service + command, then a line every 10,000 calls with the count, so a
  loop on an unimplemented function can no longer fill the log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
